Subject: popover dismissal respects the layers it opens

What: an interaction that began inside a popover marks the next outside focus as an
adoption, and the adopted layer (a select, menu or nested popover portaled to the
body) counts as inside while it stays mounted; the body and the document are never
adopted (popover-dismissal.ts, unit tested). The surface paints from the overlay roles.
Why: measured in the Tasks Filter popover, the project select's listbox mounted,
took focus, and the popover unmounted before it painted, by mouse and keyboard. A
browser moves focus to the body when the focused element is removed; adopting the
body made every node "inside" and nothing could dismiss the popover again.

